essman alex  mooney who voted against the  infrastructure bill saying the price tag  was much higher than it needed to be  they want to see us fight for the  conservative agenda roads and bridges  aren't conservative well wasting  taxpayer dollars and indebting our  country is not conservative former  president donald trump opposed the  infrastructure plan and endorsed alex  mooney and he's got a  an opponent but i think mooney's going  to do real well  giving mooney a potential leg up in a  state where trump's popularity might  rival another towering figure west  virginia political analyst happy  kircheval says bringing home federal tax  dollars was typically a political winner  this has all been important and that's  how politicians have run for the year  for many many years cutting ribbons and  traditionally an endorsement from the  state's governor jim justice would move  the needle and justice endorse mckinley  you and donald trump pick different  horses in this race what do you make of  that we can't possibly see things eye to  eye all the time the infrastructure bill  provided this state with billions of  dollars for upgrades but the question is  will a vote in favor of that bill cost  the state's longest serving member of  the u.s house  his job  for cbs saturday morning scott mcfarland  morgantown west virginia
 

